00:26:26.880 --> 00:26:27.860
Here's something for you.

00:26:28.200 --> 00:26:29.980
Steering a bird or a plane is a lot...

00:26:30.060 --> 00:26:31.740
more complicated than you showed.

00:26:31.940 --> 00:26:33.960
You got that right. Take airplanes

00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:35.660
for openers. They have

00:26:35.660 --> 00:26:38.020
movable flaps on the wings as well as on the

00:26:38.020 --> 00:26:41.080
tail. Raise one flap up

00:26:41.080 --> 00:26:43.180
and the other one down, and the wing rises

00:26:43.180 --> 00:26:44.840
for a banking turn to the right.

00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:48.260
Reverse the flaps, and the plane will bank to

00:26:48.260 --> 00:26:53.540
the left. But here's something I don't get.

00:26:53.680 --> 00:26:55.030
How does a bird fly?

00:26:55.710 --> 00:26:56.590
Good question.

00:27:03.520 --> 00:27:08.980
The movement of a bird's wing is so complicated, it took stop motion photography to figure it out.

00:27:10.020 --> 00:27:13.400
Birds use their wings both for a lift and for a push forward.

00:27:14.740 --> 00:27:19.100
Roger, but you didn't say anything about the hardest part of flying, landing.

00:27:19.590 --> 00:27:21.690
Well, we showed it, but we didn't talk about it.

00:27:22.380 --> 00:27:25.760
To land, you have to slow down and fly close to the ground.

00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:29.840
Reduce your lift so you slowly sink until your wheels touch the ground.

00:27:31.980 --> 00:27:34.990
Then cut the power and apply the bus.

00:27:35.740 --> 00:27:37.380
But landing isn't always easy.

00:27:37.740 --> 00:27:39.400
Even birds mess up once in a while.

00:27:40.780 --> 00:27:41.540
Lizards, too.

00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:45.540
Hey, thanks for calling the Magic School Bus.

00:27:45.760 --> 00:27:47.660
Keep watching and keep them flying.

00:28:00.572 --> 00:28:01.172
Death and...

00:28:30.252 --> 00:28:32.012
Inside, it's a wild garage.
